          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is open area in perforated metal panels?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Open area is the percentage of a perforated sheet that is empty space. It is calculated from hole size, spacing and layout, and it decides how much light, air and view pass through the panel."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What open area percentage is best for a facade?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the goal. Roughly 10% to 25% suits privacy and strong shade, 25% to 40% gives a balance of light and view, and above 40% suits ventilation. Always confirm with a mock-up."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the minimum hole size for perforated metal?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For punched perforations, the diameter is generally kept at or above the sheet thickness. Laser cutting can go smaller, but very fine patterns in thick sheet raise cost and cutting time."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are perforated metal panels good for Indian weather?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, when specified well. Use durable coatings with protected edges, plan for dust cleaning, and detail against birds. Perforated screens also help reduce direct sun on walls behind them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can perforated panels be backlit?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Place LED strips far enough behind the panel to produce an even glow and choose warm or neutral white to suit the finish. Plan power and cable routes at the design stage."
          }
        },
